From 9f08c0f23bba159cefcf7b48f5297d122d3e9288 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:27:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge, VideoRenderers, windowing/gbm: a picture for
 output as HDR10 kept as the codes of a 10-bit window

Dolby Vision shown as HDR10 (and an HDR10 or HLG picture mapped to SDR) is
drawn into a float texture of the size of the output, RGBA32F: 133 MB at
3840x2160, two of them (the one shown and the one being drawn), and the
copy into the window reads one at every refresh (DVBridgeGLES.cpp,
CopyConversion()), also while a picture stays on the screen. Where the
window is 10-bit fixed point in full range, what the copy makes of each
value is a code of 10 bits: floor(c * 1023 + 0.5), written 1/256 of a step
above it (COPY_FRAGMENT, dvbridge_gl_pack.c).

Now such a picture is kept as those codes, in an RGB10_A2 texture
(libplacebo-9946): the output hook quantizes it as the copy does, with the
same expression on a uniform, and the copy of a code is that code. The
same bytes in the window by construction, a quarter of the memory (33 MB
per texture) and of what each copy reads (at 60 Hz, about 6 GB/s less).
dvbridge_render_hdr10_store() takes the levels of the target and the range
the copy writes (dvbridge_gl_copy_levels(), the copy's own query, now one
function that both use); Kodi tells it before each picture
(CDVBridgeGLES::SetConversionTarget()), and kodi.log says in which form the
pictures are kept when that changes. A floating-point window (NVIDIA), 8 or
12 bits, the limited range (where the copy computes from the value), a GPU
without the format, and a renderer that is not told keep the float
texture, as before. A picture kept in the other form is not copied after
the target changes: it is drawn again.

Measured on Mesa's zink with the render test of the bridge (6 pictures of
a profile 7 FEL stream, the composer of CCM 001 and libplacebo's
reshaping): the 10-bit window from the codes and from the float texture,
248 832 000 words in 30 pictures, with each output hook (as it is, mapped
to a display of 600 cd/m2, to SDR, and a plain HDR10 picture as it is and
mapped to SDR): 0 differ; with the quantization cut off instead of rounded
(a mutation), 198 241 465 differ. Every other line of the test, the same.
